IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-income-tax`

-- Kansas income tax act -- the seat of the individual taxpayer.
--
-- "Am I a Kansas resident? Must I file? When are my return and my tax due? What is my Kansas AGI and taxable income? How
-- much do I owe, or get back? What are my earned income and senior property tax credits?" Every answer is built from the
-- rules in ks-income-tax.l4. Federal figures are asked as facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Kansas income tax -- my questions`

§§ `Am I a resident`

@export Am I a Kansas resident for Kansas income tax (K.S.A. 79-32,109(b))?
GIVEN `Kansas is my domicile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Kansas is your domicile: your permanent home, to which you intend to return
      `I spent more than six months of the year in Kansas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you spent, in total, more than six months of the tax year in Kansas
      `I can prove I am not a resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you spent more than six months in Kansas but are domiciled elsewhere: whether you can prove you are not a Kansas resident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Kansas resident` IF
    `is a resident individual` `Kansas is my domicile` `I spent more than six months of the year in Kansas` `I can prove I am not a resident`

§§ `My Kansas income`

@export What is my Kansas adjusted gross income (K.S.A. 79-32,117)?
GIVEN `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in dollars (on a joint return, the joint figure)
      `my interest from other states' bonds not in federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on bonds of states other than Kansas, or their cities and counties, that is not in your federal AGI
      `my interest from US government obligations` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on US Treasury and other federal obligations included in your federal AGI
      `my federal or military retirement pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal civil service retirement annuities and retirement pay for service in the US armed forces, included in federal AGI
      `my social security benefits in federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc The social security benefits included in your federal AGI
      `my other Kansas-exempt income` IS A NUMBER @desc Other amounts in federal AGI that a Kansas law exempts from Kansas income tax (for example KPERS retirement benefits); 0 if none
      `my other Kansas additions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other addition required by K.S.A. 79-32,117(b) (not worked out here); usually 0
      `my other Kansas subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other subtraction allowed by K.S.A. 79-32,117(c) (not worked out here); usually 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Kansas adjusted gross income` MEANS
    `Kansas adjusted gross income` (`Kansas adjusted gross income facts` WITH
        `federal adjusted gross income` IS `my federal adjusted gross income`
        `interest on other states' and their subdivisions' obligations not in federal AGI` IS `my interest from other states' bonds not in federal AGI`
        `interest on United States obligations in federal AGI` IS `my interest from US government obligations`
        `federal civil service and military retirement benefits` IS `my federal or military retirement pay`
        `social security benefits in federal AGI` IS `my social security benefits in federal AGI`
        `amounts exempt from Kansas income tax under other Kansas laws` IS `my other Kansas-exempt income`
        `other additions` IS `my other Kansas additions`
        `other subtractions` IS `my other Kansas subtractions`)

@export What is my Kansas taxable income, taking the larger of the Kansas standard and itemized deductions (K.S.A. 79-32,116 to 79-32,121b)?
GIVEN `my Kansas adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Kansas adjusted gross income (K.S.A. 79-32,117)
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return
      `my federal additional standard deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many federal additional standard deductions you (and your spouse) are allowed for being 65 or older or blind: 0 to 4
      `my federal dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents you may claim for federal income tax
      `of those, born in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those dependents were born during the tax year
      `stillbirth certificates issued to me in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc As a parent, the number of certificates of stillbirth issued in the tax year (0 if none)
      `my charitable gifts` IS A NUMBER @desc Charitable contributions deductible under IRC s170
      `my medical expenses deductible federally` IS A NUMBER @desc Medical care expenses allowable as a deduction under IRC s213 (the part above the federal floor)
      `my mortgage interest` IS A NUMBER @desc Qualified residence (mortgage) interest under IRC s163(h)
      `my property taxes` IS A NUMBER @desc Taxes on real and personal property under IRC s164(a)
      `my state and local income taxes in those deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any state or local income taxes included in the deductions above (they are taken off)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my Kansas taxable income` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my filing status`
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `not covered` `a married person filing a separate return is not encoded: 79-32,119(c)(2) gives one standard deduction for "married filing status" and does not say how it applies to a separate return`
    OTHERWISE `answered` (`Kansas taxable income` `my Kansas adjusted gross income` deduction exemptions)
    WHERE
        std MEANS `Kansas standard deduction` `my filing status` `my federal additional standard deductions`
        itemized MEANS `Kansas itemized deduction` `my charitable gifts` `my medical expenses deductible federally` `my mortgage interest` `my property taxes` `my state and local income taxes in those deductions`
        deduction MEANS `Kansas deduction` (itemized GREATER THAN std) std itemized
        exemptions MEANS `Kansas personal exemptions` `my filing status` `my federal dependents` `of those, born in the year` `stillbirth certificates issued to me in the year`

§§ `Must I file, and by when`

@export Must I make a Kansas income tax return (K.S.A. 79-3220(a))?
GIVEN `I must file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to file a federal income tax return for the year
      `my gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income for the year (on a joint return, both spouses')
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `my federal additional standard deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many federal additional standard deductions you (and your spouse) are allowed for being 65 or older or blind
      `my federal dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents you may claim for federal income tax
      `my only Kansas income is from an electing pass-through entity and I am a nonresident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a nonresident whose only Kansas income is from a pass-through entity that elected to pay the tax under the SALT parity act
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Must I make a Kansas return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my filing status`
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `not covered` `a married person filing a separate return is not encoded: 79-32,119(c)(2) gives one standard deduction for "married filing status" and does not say how it applies to a separate return`
    OTHERWISE `answered` (`shall make a return` `I must file a federal return` `my gross income` std exemption `my only Kansas income is from an electing pass-through entity and I am a nonresident`)
    WHERE
        std MEANS `Kansas standard deduction` `my filing status` `my federal additional standard deductions`
        exemption MEANS `Kansas personal exemptions` `my filing status` `my federal dependents` 0 0

@export By what date must I file my Kansas income tax return (K.S.A. 79-3221(b), (c)(3))?
GIVEN `the month my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The month your tax year ends, 1 to 12 (12 for a calendar year)
      `the year my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The year your tax year ends
      `the IRS extended my federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the IRS granted you an extension of time to file your federal return
      `my extended federal due date` IS A DATE @desc If the IRS extended your federal return: the extended federal due date
GIVETH A DATE
`When must I file my Kansas return` MEANS
    IF `the IRS extended my federal return`
    THEN `my extended federal due date`
    ELSE `the 15th day of the fourth month following` `the month my tax year ends` `the year my tax year ends`

@export By what date must I pay my Kansas income tax (K.S.A. 79-3225)?
GIVEN `the month my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The month your tax year ends, 1 to 12 (12 for a calendar year)
      `the year my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The year your tax year ends
      `months the director extended payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Months by which the director of taxation extended the time to pay (0 if none; at most 6 unless you are abroad)
GIVETH A DATE
`When must I pay my Kansas tax` MEANS
    IF `months the director extended payment` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the 15th day of the fourth month following` `the month my tax year ends` `the year my tax year ends`
    ELSE `the 15th day of the fourth month following` (`the month my tax year ends` PLUS `months the director extended payment`) `the year my tax year ends`

§§ `How much do I owe, or get back`

@export How much Kansas income tax do I owe for the year, or how much is refunded, after credits and the tax already withheld (K.S.A. 79-32,110, 79-32,111c, 79-32,205, 79-32,263, 79-3225)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year (2025 or later)
      `I was a Kansas resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Kansas resident for the whole year (a nonresident or part-year resident answers no)
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status
      `my Kansas adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Kansas adjusted gross income (K.S.A. 79-32,117)
      `my Kansas taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Kansas taxable income (K.S.A. 79-32,116)
      `my Kansas-source income` IS A NUMBER @desc If you were not a resident all year: your modified Kansas source income (for a part-year resident, including all income of the resident period); otherwise the same as your Kansas AGI
      `I paid income tax to another state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a Kansas resident, you paid income tax to another state on income included in Kansas AGI
      `the secretary published a rate reduction for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the secretary of revenue has certified and published an income tax rate reduction under K.S.A. 79-32,110c for this tax year
      `I am a 100% disabled veteran` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an honorably discharged veteran receiving VA disability compensation at the 100% rate for a permanent service-connected disability
      `valid social security numbers are on my return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your return gives a valid social security number for you, your spouse and every dependent
      `I had a valid social security number all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a valid social security number for the whole year
      `my spouse had one all year and we file jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you file jointly and your spouse held a valid social security number for the whole year
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal earned income credit (IRC s32)
      `my federal child and dependent care credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal child and dependent care credit allowed against your federal tax (IRC s21)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age at the end of the tax year
      `my household income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household income for the senior property tax credit (all household members' income, including social security)
      `the federal poverty level for two persons` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal poverty guideline for a household of two for the year
      `property taxes I paid on my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Property taxes you actually and timely paid on your principal residence
      `I got a homestead refund for my home this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received a Kansas homestead property tax refund for the same home for the year
      `Kansas tax withheld and estimated tax paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Kansas income tax withheld from your pay and any Kansas estimated tax you paid
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What do I owe or get back in Kansas` MEANS
    IF `the tax year` LESS THAN 2025
    THEN `not covered` `tax years before 2025 are not encoded: the 2025 exemption amounts of 79-32,121 and 79-32,121b are the ones encoded`
    ELSE IF `the secretary published a rate reduction for the year`
         THEN `not covered` `a rate reduction certified and published by the secretary of revenue under 79-32,110c is not encoded: the rates would be those the secretary published`
         ELSE IF `I am a 100% disabled veteran`
              THEN `not covered` `the additional exemption of a 100% disabled veteran is not encoded: 79-32,121(b) gives $2,250 and 79-32,121b(b)(2) gives $2,320 for the same person, and the two 2025 Acts are not reconciled in the deposited text`
              ELSE IF `I paid income tax to another state`
                   THEN `not covered` `the credit for income tax paid to another state (79-32,111(a)) is not encoded`
                   ELSE CONSIDER `my filing status`
                        WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `not covered` `a married person filing a separate return is not encoded: 79-32,119(c)(2) gives one standard deduction for "married filing status" and does not say how it applies to a separate return`
                        OTHERWISE `answered` (`tax to be paid after the 79-3225(a) cancellation` balance)
    WHERE
        residentTax MEANS `tax under the 79-32,110(a) schedule` `my filing status` `my Kansas taxable income`
        tax MEANS IF `I was a Kansas resident all year` THEN residentTax ELSE `nonresident tax` residentTax `my Kansas-source income` `my Kansas adjusted gross income`
        creditsOk MEANS `credits are allowed under 79-32,265` `valid social security numbers are on my return` `I had a valid social security number all year` `my spouse had one all year and we file jointly`
        careCredit MEANS IF creditsOk AND `I was a Kansas resident all year` THEN `Kansas child and dependent care credit before the limit` `my federal child and dependent care credit` ELSE 0
        eitc MEANS IF creditsOk AND `I was a Kansas resident all year` THEN `Kansas earned income credit` `my federal earned income credit` ELSE 0
        safesr MEANS IF creditsOk THEN `SAFESR credit` `my age` `my household income` `the federal poverty level for two persons` `property taxes I paid on my home` `I got a homestead refund for my home this year` ELSE 0
        balance MEANS (`tax after credits` tax careCredit (eitc PLUS safesr)) MINUS `Kansas tax withheld and estimated tax paid`

§§ `My credits`

@export How much is my Kansas earned income credit, which is refundable (K.S.A. 79-32,205)?
GIVEN `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal earned income credit (IRC s32), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Kansas earned income credit` MEANS `Kansas earned income credit` `my federal earned income credit`

-- Only for a person 65 or older who owns and lives in their home.
@export How much is my SAFESR credit, the refundable senior property tax credit (K.S.A. 79-32,263)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in the tax year
      `my household income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household income: all household members' income for the calendar year, including social security
      `the federal poverty level for two persons` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal poverty guideline for a household of two for the year
      `property taxes I paid on my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Property taxes you actually and timely paid on your principal residence
      `I got a homestead refund for my home this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received a Kansas homestead property tax refund for the same home for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my SAFESR credit` MEANS
    `SAFESR credit` `my age` `my household income` `the federal poverty level for two persons` `property taxes I paid on my home` `I got a homestead refund for my home this year`
